# The score from a normal game start (seed 1, the south coast village): it wakes
# with the coast's drone and air, the arrival phrase plays, the pad and then the
# calm pulse come in; the machines' works yard brings in the installation's grid under it;
# there a runner that has seen the player quickens that pulse and raises the
# dissonance, and the score resolves once the runner is gone. A layer counts
# once it plays at 75_music's HEARD share of its level. Stems bake while it
# runs, so it is slow on a first run and quick once the disk cache holds them.
# The log shows every layer entering and leaving ("tour score ...").
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=900 tools/tour.sh tours/score.tour
coast calm
await score 150
shot 01-the-score-wakes
await score_phrase 90
await score_pad 300
shot 02-the-pad-has-come
await score_pulse 300
shot 03-the-pulse-plays
# To the machines' works, by name, and under the nearest thing of theirs that
# hums: the walk here was three hand-timed run legs from the spawn to a pylon
# fifty tiles east, on a world long since regrown; they ended at the village's
# shore, and the nearest installation is now the first works yard's (the story's
# `the_yard`, where the Tide Reaper keeps its rows), 276 tiles off.
at stood:the_yard
wait 0.6
near pylon,relay,intake,pump_house,conveyor,stack
wait 0.5
await score_grid 60
shot 04-under-the-works with score_grid
spawn runner
await score_tense 90
await score_dissonance 60
shot 05-a-machine-closing-in with mob:runner
coast calm
await score_resolve 120
shot 06-resolved
